meta {
  name: List
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/web/bestelorder?pageSize=10
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  pageSize: 10
  ~levnr:
  ~ordnr:
  ~naam:
  ~sortField:
  ~sortDir:
  ~page:
}

headers {
  X-Auth-Token: {{authToken}}
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  Lists bestelorder (purchase order to supplier/leverancier - the `order`
  table) rows, paged, newest ordnr first by default. Query params: levnr
  (exact match, 0/absent = no filter), ordnr (prefix match on the string
  form, absent = no filter), naam (substring match on the leverancier
  name, case-insensitive, absent = no filter), sortField (one of "ordnr",
  "datum", "naam", "stempel"; absent/unrecognized falls back to "ordnr"),
  sortDir ("asc" or "desc"; absent/unrecognized falls back to "desc"),
  page (default 1), pageSize (default 25, max 200). Unlike /web/bon,
  invalid/non-numeric levnr/page/pageSize are NOT rejected with 400 - they
  silently fall back to "no filter"/default (same approach as /web/klant
  and /web/offerte). Response includes hasMore instead of an exact
  totalCount - see Backend/README.md for why - plus the effective
  sortField/sortDir that were applied. Read-only - no POST/PUT/DELETE,
  BestelorderBE has no write methods at all. Backed by
  Backend/src/Luna/Web/BestelorderHandler.cls +
  Luna/BusinessLogic/BestelorderBE.cls.
}
